# GUIDANCE

> **Reference** for the RGV loop (DRY source), per-artifact extraction patterns, few-shot examples, BizTalk→MuleSoft decision matrices, Mermaid standards, and the quality checklist.

---

## SECTION 1: RGV LOOP (DRY SOURCE)

The single authoritative definition. All phases reference here.

```
FOR EACH section (orchestration / schema / map / pipeline / helper):
  1. RE-READ   — Fresh Read tool call on ALL relevant artifact files
  2. INVENTORY — Count target elements, list names, COMMIT to count N
  3. GENERATE  — Produce section content with EXACTLY N items
  4. VERIFY    — Count generated items, compare to N → "Processed N/N"
  5. FIX       — If mismatch, RE-READ source, find missing, fix BEFORE proceeding
  6. CHECKPOINT— Emit count-verified micro-checkpoint, write to file, proceed
```

**Why:** Each section is an ATOMIC UNIT. Do not start section N+1 until section N passes verification. This prevents summarization — the root cause of missed shapes and map links.

**Evidence-Bound rule:** every extracted item cites its source — `Source: Process_X.odx, OID a782...` or `Source: Map_Y.xsl, LinkID 4`. If you cannot cite a source, it is an ⚠️ ASSUMPTION or 🔴 GAP, not a fact.

