## SECTION 2: ARTIFACT EXTRACTION PATTERNS

### `.odx` Orchestrations
BizTalk designer XML (`om:Element` tree). Extract:
- `ServiceDeclaration` → orchestration name, type modifier, invokable, activation.
- `VariableDeclaration` / `MessageDeclaration` → name, .NET/schema `Type`, direction.
- `ServiceBody` statements in order: `Receive` (PortName, Activate, `DNFPredicate` filters), `Send`, `Construct` (+ `Transform` ClassName = map, `MessageAssignment` expression), `Call`/`CallExternal` (Invokee = helper), `Decision`/`Rule`, `Loop`, `Scope`/`Catch`, `Parallel`.
- Inline expression code is in `Property Name="Expression"` (decode `&quot;`, `&#xD;&#xA;`). Capture verbatim.
- Ports: `PortDeclaration` / port-type bindings.

### `.btm` Maps (UTF-16) + `.xsl`
- `.btm` is UTF-16 — decode first. Contains `<SrcTree>`/`<TrgTree>` references, `<Links>` (LinkFrom/LinkTo XPaths), `<Functoids>` (Functoid-FID, parameters, constants), and `<CustomXSLT XsltPath=...>` when custom XSLT is used.
- **Prefer the paired `.xsl`** for actual transform logic; use `.btm` for functoid intent and constant values.
- Document EVERY link: source XPath → target XPath, plus functoid logic (e.g., FID 107 = scripting functoid with inline value).

### `.xsd` Schemas
- Often UTF-16. Extract target namespace, root node, element/attribute tree with types and occurrence. Note EDI/flat-file annotations (`b:` BizTalk schema extensions) when present.

### `.btp` Pipelines
- Stages (Decode, Disassemble, Validate, ResolveParty / PreAssemble, Assemble, Encode) → component list per stage with key properties.

### `.cs` Helpers
- Class + public methods (signatures). Summarize logic and include the complete code block. Common types: crypto/signing, XML canonicalization, config/section-handler readers, email senders. These are CALLED by orchestration `Call`/expression statements — link call-sites.

### `.btproj` / `.sln`
- Project list, output assembly names, referenced assemblies (incl. external ones whose source may be absent).

