## SECTION 3: FEW-SHOT EXAMPLES (❌ BAD → ✅ GOOD)

### Map documentation
❌ BAD:
```
Map_824in_to_Email: maps the 824 to an email. Sets subject and body.
```
✅ GOOD:
```
Map_824in_to_Email (Map_824in_to_Email.btm + .xsl) — 5/5 links
| Link | Source XPath | Target XPath | Logic |
|------|--------------|--------------|-------|
| 1 | .../ST/ST01 | (functoid 107 input) | Scripting functoid, const "123qwe" |
| 2 | functoid 1 out | /Email/Subject | value from functoid |
| 3 | functoid 1 out | /Email/Body | value from functoid |
| 4 | functoid 1 out | /Email/SendToList/SendTo | value from functoid |
| 5 | functoid 1 out | /Email/SendCcList/SendCc | value from functoid |
Source: Map_824in_to_Email.btm (UTF-16) + Map_824in_to_Email.xsl
```
**Why:** GOOD documents every link with XPaths + functoid logic + source — reproducible. BAD summarizes and loses the mapping.

### Orchestration inline expression
❌ BAD: `Get config — reads some settings.`
✅ GOOD:
```
Shape "Get config" (VariableAssignment, OID acf4...):
  RunEnv  = Venture.Utilities.ConfigHelper.GetNameValueFileSectionHandlerKey("RuntimeEnvironment","VenHPEdiSettings");
  strEmailTo = ...GetNameValueFileSectionHandlerKey("EmailRecipientTo","VenHPEdiSettings");
🔴 GAP: ConfigHelper source not in export → MuleSoft needs an equivalent config/property lookup.
```
**Why:** Captures verbatim logic + the helper dependency + the replication implication.

### Helper with absent source
❌ BAD: invent what `CryptoHelper.Sign()` probably does.
✅ GOOD: `CryptoHelper.Sign(doc, cert) — called by _signSubmission.odx. Source: CryptoHelper.cs (present)` OR if absent: `🔴 GAP: assembly Venture.Utilities referenced by 3 orchestrations; source not in export.`

