## SECTION 4: BIZTALK → MULESOFT DECISION MATRIX

| BizTalk Construct | MuleSoft Equivalent | Notes |
|-------------------|---------------------|-------|
| Receive port + location | Listener (HTTP/File/SFTP/JMS) source | Adapter type from port binding |
| Send port | Outbound connector / `<*:request>` | |
| Orchestration | Mule flow / sub-flow | Shapes → flow components |
| Receive (Activate) | Flow trigger | |
| Construct + Transform (map) | `<ee:transform>` (DataWeave) | Map logic → DataWeave |
| `.btm`/`.xsl` map | DataWeave script | XSLT may be portable directly |
| Decision shape | `<choice>` | DNF predicate → condition |
| Loop shape | `<foreach>` / `<parallel-foreach>` | |
| Scope + Catch | `<try>` + error handlers | |
| Call .NET helper | DataWeave fn / Java invoke / connector | 🔴 if source absent |
| Correlation sets | Correlation / object store | |
| Pipeline (disassemble/validate) | Listener + transform + schema validation | |
| Schema (.xsd) | DataWeave type / schema validation | EDI → EDI connector |
| AS2 / EDI X12 | AnypointMQ + EDI / X12 connector | |

> **Tree of Thought for ambiguous mappings:** evaluate ≥2 MuleSoft options, pick one, note the trade-off. E.g., "Loop with DB calls → Branch A `foreach` (ordered, simpler) vs Branch B `parallel-foreach` (faster, order not guaranteed). Chosen: A — original orchestration is sequential."

