## SECTION 5: REPLICATION-READINESS VERDICTS

| Verdict | Meaning | Trigger |
|---------|---------|---------|
| 🟢 Replicable | Full source present; clean MuleSoft mapping exists | All referenced artifacts present |
| 🟡 Ambiguous | Replicable but needs a decision/clarification | Dense functoids, env-specific binding, design choice |
| 🔴 Blocked | Cannot fully replicate from provided source | Absent assembly/schema, encrypted value, runtime-only binding |

Every 🟡/🔴 MUST appear in `replication-gap-report.md` with reason + recommended action.

---

## SECTION 6: MERMAID DIAGRAM STANDARDS

- Put `%%{ init: { 'flowchart': { 'curve': 'linear' } } }%%` atop every `flowchart`/`graph`.
- Use `<br/>` for line breaks in labels, NEVER `\n`.
- `stateDiagram-v2`: `[*]` start/end, transitions labeled with trigger events, states in workflow order.
- One Mermaid flow per orchestration (Section 3): nodes = shapes in execution order, branches for Decision/Parallel; dashed `-.->` for catch/back-edges.
- Color by semantic role (Material 200/300): sources, transforms, decisions, sends — not alphabetically; declare `style` lines at the end.
- Run a render self-check: balanced brackets, no stray `\n`, every node referenced.

